% Text built-ins. Everything counts code points; positions are 1-based and 0
% means "not found".

### name: txt.len
--- source
LEN("Zażółć")
--- expect
num 6
===
### name: txt.len.astral
--- note
Two code points, four UTF-8 bytes, three UTF-16 units. LEN counts code points.
--- source
LEN("👍a")
--- expect
num 2
===
### name: txt.left
--- source
LEFT("Zażółć", 3)
--- expect
text "Zaż"
===
### name: txt.left.astral
--- source
LEFT("👍ab", 1)
--- expect
text "👍"
===
### name: txt.left.beyond-end
--- source
LEFT("ab", 9)
--- expect
text "ab"
===
### name: txt.right
--- source
RIGHT("👍ab", 2)
--- expect
text "ab"
===
### name: txt.substr
--- source
SUBSTR("abcdef", 3, 2)
--- expect
text "cd"
===
### name: txt.substr.to-end
--- source
SUBSTR("abcdef", 4)
--- expect
text "def"
===
### name: txt.substr.is-one-based
--- source
SUBSTR("abc", 0, 1)
--- expect
error E_RANGE
===
### name: txt.find
--- source
FIND("ż", "Zażółć")
--- expect
num 3
===
### name: txt.find.not-found-is-zero
--- source
FIND("q", "abc")
--- expect
num 0
===
### name: txt.find.from
--- source
FIND("a", "banana", 4)
--- expect
num 4
===
### name: txt.find.empty-needle
--- source
FIND("", "abc")
--- expect
error E_BAD_ARG
===
### name: txt.replace
--- source
REPLACE("a", "X", "banana")
--- expect
text "bXnXnX"
===
### name: txt.replace.non-overlapping
--- source
REPLACE("aa", "b", "aaaa")
--- expect
text "bb"
===
### name: txt.replace.empty-needle
--- source
REPLACE("", "x", "abc")
--- expect
error E_BAD_ARG
===
### name: txt.split
--- source
SPLIT("a,b,c", ",")
--- expect
tree -{"1"=t"a", "2"=t"b", "3"=t"c"}
===
### name: txt.split.trailing-separator
--- source
SPLIT("a,", ",")
--- expect
tree -{"1"=t"a", "2"=t""}
===
### name: txt.split.empty-separator
--- source
SPLIT("abc", "")
--- expect
error E_BAD_ARG
===
### name: txt.trim
--- source
"[" & TRIM("  a b \t") & "]"
--- expect
text "[a b]"
===
### name: txt.ltrim
--- source
"[" & LTRIM("  a  ") & "]"
--- expect
text "[a  ]"
===
### name: txt.rtrim
--- source
"[" & RTRIM("  a  ") & "]"
--- expect
text "[  a]"
===
### name: txt.upper.ascii-only
--- note
Ä is left alone on purpose: PHP's strtoupper and JS's toUpperCase cannot be
made to agree above ASCII, so SEL does not pretend they can.
--- source
UPPER("aÄz")
--- expect
text "AÄZ"
===
### name: txt.lower.ascii-only
--- source
LOWER("AÄZ")
--- expect
text "aÄz"
===
### name: txt.backwards
--- source
BACKWARDS("ab👍")
--- expect
text "👍ba"
===
### name: txt.repeat
--- source
REPEAT("ab", 3)
--- expect
text "ababab"
===
### name: txt.repeat.zero
--- source
"[" & REPEAT("ab", 0) & "]"
--- expect
text "[]"
===
