### name: txt.rejects-binary
--- note
Text functions do not silently decode bytes; FROM_UTF8 is the explicit door.
--- source
LEN(FROM_HEX("41"))
--- expect
error E_NOT_TEXT
===
### name: txt.substr.length-beyond-any-string
--- note
A length larger than the string returns the rest of it. In C++ the count
saturates at the maximum integer, so `start + len` was signed overflow and
returned "" instead.
--- source
SUBSTR("abcdef", 2, 9223372036854775807)
--- expect
text "bcdef"
===
### name: txt.find.start-beyond-any-string
--- source
FIND("ab", "abc", 9223372036854775807)
--- expect
num 0
===
### name: num.round.scale-out-of-range
--- note
A scale no implementation could allocate must fail loudly rather than being
truncated into a small one. C++ cast it to int, wrapping 4294967296 to 0 and
answering `2` with total confidence.
--- source
ROUND(1.5, 4294967296)
--- expect
error E_RANGE
===
